# rns510-flashkit: read-only unit profile dump -> SD card (/sda)
# Commands below are confirmed present in the SWL loader's VxWorks shell
# (hdTermShow*, dosFsShow, iosDevShow, devs). OUTPUT CAPTURE is the one
# unvalidated part: VxWorks shell has no ">" redirect. Two strategies, test both:
#   A) run the show cmds (they print to serial + InfoLog), then copy InfoLog to SD
#   B) the loader has a built-in /sda/trace/ path; enabling trace may capture it
#
# Create the output dir on SD first.
mkdir("/sda/profile")

# --- storage devices + partitions ---
iosDevShow
devs
hdTermShowDeviceIdentification
hdTermShowDeviceStatus
hdTermShowApplRegisterStatus

# --- filesystem per partition (sizes, FS type, free space) ---
dosFsShow "/hdb1"
dosFsShow "/hdb2"
dosFsShow "/hdb3"

# --- raw MBR (first sector) of the master device, for exact partition geometry ---
# (device node name confirmed at runtime from iosDevShow; adjust if different)
# copy the first 512 bytes of the whole-disk device to SD:
# cp "/ataMaster", "/sda/profile/mbr.bin"   # validate device name on unit

# --- coding / registers (CTEST.OUT already loaded by DLSCRIPT) ---
# ReadRegData / TestCoding dump current coding array:
TestCoding(0x400)
ReadRegData(0x21)
ReadRegData(0x0B3A)

# --- flush InfoLog so the above is persisted, then copy it to SD ---
IL_Flush
# copy("/tffs0/data/diag/cfg/InfoLog", "/sda/profile/infolog.txt")  # validate path
IL_Flush
